# Build context of the frontend image. The build stage does `COPY . .`, so everything not excluded here
# ends up in a layer — and Vite reads .env files at build time, which would bake their values into the bundle.
node_modules
dist
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment: Vite would read it and inline it into the built assets
.env
.env.*

# Credentials of a registry, and anything that looks like a key
.npmrc
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx

# Leftovers and logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*~
coverage

# Assistant context: never in an image layer
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
